content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Member",
      "description": "Person who holds a gym membership and uses gym services.",
      "attributes": [
        "Membership Record"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Membership Record",
      "description": "Stored information about a member’s membership status and history."
    },
    {
      "name": "Sign Up",
      "description": "Action and data submitted to start a new membership."
    },
    {
      "name": "Fitness Class",
      "description": "A scheduled group training session offered by the gym.",
      "attributes": [
        "Attendance",
        "Capacity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Attendance",
      "description": "Count of members who attend a fitness class."
    },
    {
      "name": "Capacity",
      "description": "Maximum number of members allowed in a fitness class."
    },
    {
      "name": "Pause Request",
      "description": "Member’s request to temporarily freeze their membership."
    },
    {
      "name": "Front Desk Staff",
      "description": "Staff responsible for membership handling and customer requests."
    },
    {
      "name": "Member Complaint",
      "description": "A complaint submitted by a member about gym issues."
    },
    {
      "name": "Trainer",
      "description": "Gym professional who conducts classes and personal training."
    },
    {
      "name": "Weekly Timetable",
      "description": "List of all scheduled fitness classes for the week.",
      "attributes": [
        "Fitness Class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Workout Plan",
      "description": "A personalized training plan created by a trainer."
    },
    {
      "name": "Personal Training Session",
      "description": "An individual training appointment between a trainer and a member."
    },
    {
      "name": "Facility Manager",
      "description": "Staff responsible for equipment maintenance and facilities."
    },
    {
      "name": "Gym Equipment",
      "description": "Exercise machines and equipment available in the gym.",
      "attributes": [
        "Status"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Status",
      "description": "Current condition or usability state of equipment."
    },
    {
      "name": "Repair Order",
      "description": "Request issued to repair malfunctioning gym equipment."
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Reception": {
      "objects": [
        "Member",
        "Front Desk Staff",
        "Sign Up",
        "Membership Record",
        "Pause Request",
        "Member Complaint"
      ]
    },
    "Fitness Classes": {
      "objects": [
        "Trainer",
        "Weekly Timetable",
        "Fitness Class",
        "Attendance",
        "Capacity"
      ]
    },
    "Personal Training": {
      "objects": [
        "Trainer",
        "Personal Training Session",
        "Workout Plan",
        "Membership Record"
      ]
    },
    "Facility Management": {
      "objects": [
        "Facility Manager",
        "Repair Order",
        "Gym Equipment",
        "Status"
      ]
    },
    "subdomain connections": [
      "Reception--Fitness Classes",
      "Reception--Personal Training",
      "Reception--Facility Management"
    ]
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Reception": {
      "derived from": "Reception Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Member",
        "Front Desk Staff",
        "Sign Up",
        "Membership Record",
        "Pause Request",
        "Member Complaint"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Fitness Classes": {
      "derived from": "Fitness Classes Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Trainer",
        "Weekly Timetable",
        "Fitness Class",
        "Attendance",
        "Capacity"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Personal Training": {
      "derived from": "Personal Training Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Personal Trainer",
        "Personal Training Session",
        "Workout Plan",
        "Member Performance Record"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Trainer -> Personal Trainer",
        "Membership Record -> Member Performance Record"
      ]
    },
    "Facility Management": {
      "derived from": "Facility Management Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Facility Manager",
        "Repair Order",
        "Gym Equipment",
        "Status"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
